@nsobid-97F9664CFB2721546954CDEB3B303A4C

# Super Mario RPG 1.0.1 - 8192x8192 shadow resolution

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces the sun (main light) shadow map to 8192x8192 and the character
// shadow decal atlas to 4096x4096.
//
// The sun shadow size comes from the active URP pipeline asset, which the
// game swaps per scene through its quality levels: 2048 in most scenes
// (UniversalRP-sr2k_sd72_cc4), 1024 in some (UniversalRP-sr1k_sd72_cc4),
// split into up to 4 cascades. URP copies the asset value into the per-frame
// shadow data in UniversalRenderPipeline.InitializeShadowData; overriding
// those two reads applies the size in every scene and quality level, and
// MainLightShadowCasterPass uses it without any further clamp.
//
// Characters cast a separate projected "fake" shadow (UTJ FakeShadowPass),
// drawn into one shared decal atlas for up to 25 characters. Its size,
// decalMapSize, is 2048 in the renderer data and only sets the texture
// dimensions; shadows are placed in normalized coordinates, so a larger
// atlas sharpens them with no other change. 4096 already gives each
// character more texels than it can show.
//
// Point and spot light shadows (additional lights) are left as shipped.

@enabled
// UniversalRenderPipeline.InitializeShadowData:
// mainLightShadowmapWidth / Height (was LDR W9,[X20,#0x7C], asset value)
019B95C4 09008452   // MOVZ W9,#8192
019B95CC 09008452   // MOVZ W9,#8192
// FakeShadowPassFeature.CharacterShadowPass.OnCameraSetup:
// decal atlas size (was LDR W1,[X0,#0xDC], decalMapSize 2048)
01EC7E88 01008252   // MOVZ W1,#4096
@stop

// Reverse-engineered against Super Mario RPG 1.0.1 (Unity 2021.3.15f1, URP,
// IL2CPP). Names come from the game's own IL2CPP metadata; every offset was
// byte-verified against the IDB.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
